Id: node-krea2-anypaint
Title: Krea 2 AnyPaint
Does: Adds arbitrary-mask inpainting and outpainting on Krea 2 Turbo in a single graph -- paint any shape (or
 several disconnected regions) to change, or extend the canvas on any side, and one LoRA fills it while every
 unpainted pixel is preserved. The krea2-anypaint inpaint and outpaint workflows do not appear without it.
Target: custom_nodes/krea2-anypaint
Source: https://github.com/alexw5702-afk/krea2-anypaint
Rev: 675be5a91eadbf8b8997b21c0e8e1848310b9571
Why: Registers Krea2AnyPaintPrepare / Krea2AnyPaintEncode / Krea2AnyPaintModelPatch (MIT, alexw5702-afk), which
 drive the yijunwang2 AnyPaint LoRA: Prepare builds the padded known canvas plus the generate/keep masks and a
 384px semantic reference; Encode attaches the reference latents and a token-aligned noise_mask; ModelPatch
 registers the reference over the target grid and caches its isolated K/V. Preservation is per-step (the sampler
 pins known tokens each denoise step), so there is no paste-back composite. A hard requirement of the
 krea2-anypaint inpaint/outpaint workflows -- without this pack they stay unavailable.
Provides: krea2-anypaint-nodes
---
